.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Anchored to any depth, not just the root: a parallel localdev checkout
# (a git worktree, a second clone for a bisect) sitting under the context
# root brings its own node_modules and .venv with it, and a root-only
# pattern lets all of that into the build context. One such checkout is
# ~550MB; the symptom is a build that spends its first minute on
# "transferring context".
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/worktrees/
web/dist/
docs/
tests/
data/
certs/
notes/
nginx/
# sheaf_dev/ intentionally NOT ignored - needs to be in build context
# so the INCLUDE_DEV_TOOLS build arg can conditionally install it.
# It is only installed when INCLUDE_DEV_TOOLS=true; otherwise deleted.

__pycache__
*.pyc
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache

*.md
LICENSE
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
